+# Final review, cluster 1 (misc), epic hg-k4l
+
+## Source and method
+
+- Range: base 0dbe4772f4cd541e6b5ecaa1dd55b9a72f62c784, head efc21b65eb225578d3a623b29f23b3688849ea8b. Both verified with `git rev-parse --verify <sha>^{commit}`.
+- Caller checkout observed at HEAD efc21b65eb225578d3a623b29f23b3688849ea8b, branch super-auto/seat-failure-manager-seats, working tree clean. The review made no checkout changes and created no worktree. All reads came from `git show <head>:<path>`.
+- Cluster files: `.gitignore`, `CURRENT-DESIGN.md`, `skills/seat/SKILL.md` (slices 000001, 000002, 000021).
+- Spec: `bd show hg-k4l` and docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-05-seat-failure-manager-seats/2026-11-05-seat-failure-manager-seats-design.md at head. The spec has a `## Requirement baseline` section, so its human request and rows B1-B14 plus S1 are the acceptance standard.
+- Other source opened only to check named risks: src/cli/seat.rs (HOOK_PROMPT, seat_failure), src/cli/daemon_error.rs (line text), src/bootstrap/mod.rs (seat_reply manager/node_manager fields), src/observe/classify.rs and src/reconcile/desired.rs (the CURRENT-DESIGN closure claim), src/bootstrap/setup_claude.rs (skill embedding), src/bootstrap/tests.rs (skill text tests).
+- Bead tree state observed: hg-k4l.14, .17, .19, .20, .22, .24 and .25 are open; all others are closed.
+
+## Analysis of .gitignore
+
+The change adds `.superpowers/` (execution workspaces) to the ignore list. Head tracks no `.superpowers/` paths, so nothing tracked becomes ignored. Low risk and unrelated to product behaviour.
+
+## Analysis of CURRENT-DESIGN.md
+
+The dated 2026-11-05 line is what spec §4.9 requires ("CURRENT-DESIGN.md gets a dated line"). Its claims match the code at head:
+- Pane closure: classify routes the node manager's clones to `gone` and never to a Pane cascade.
+- Tab closure: the node manager seat is routed to `node_manager_gone` instead of `seat_group`.
+- Workspace closure: the node manager's teamspace goes to `gone` and is not retired. Its other seats are excluded only for the node manager itself, so they still retire one by one.
+- Reopening, workspace first: `node_manager_with_absent_runtime_gets_tab_and_panes` in src/reconcile/tests.rs checks this.
+
+The line covers B11 ("stays open, gets reopened if it ever is closed") together with the human's approval of the closure override. It does not mention the "moved outside a plan is tolerated and surfaced" rule from §4.9. That rule is not a contract the line has to state. The fuller CURRENT-DESIGN section (manager precedence, exit codes, fallback removal) belongs to open bead hg-k4l.20 and is not in this range.
+
+## Analysis of skills/seat/SKILL.md
+
+Step 1 failure branch (§4.5; B2, B3):
+- Exit 5 tells the session to show the line, carry on without seat rules, re-run `/seat` later and not repair the daemon unless instructed. This matches `SEAT_UNAVAILABLE` in src/cli/seat.rs and B3.
+- Exit 6 tells the session not to retry and to report to the node manager the line names, or to the user "when the line says so". That matches the `node_manager_suffix` forms in src/bootstrap/mod.rs: "report it to the node manager seat <name> (<id>)", "no node manager is assigned; report it to the user" and "you are the node manager seat; report it to the user".
+- Any other exit shows the line and does not guess the seat. This covers exit 2 (`NOT_IN_HERDR`, "this session has no graph seat") and exit 1.
+- HOOK_PROMPT carries the "If /seat fails, follow the skill's failure step." clause (src/cli/seat.rs:92), so the hook-to-skill handoff is wired.
+- The skill reaches agents through `include_str!` in src/bootstrap/setup_claude.rs and the `setup claude` install path, which is unchanged as §4.5 requires.
+
+Step 3 escalation (§4.5; B5):
+- The skill names `manager` and `node_manager` from the reply as the escalation targets. It lists the lifecycle classes the human gave (environment, peer conflicts, own ability to operate: usage limits, trust prompts) and the order manager, then node_manager, then user.
+- `seat_reply` at head fills `manager` (first element of `manager_chain`) and `node_manager` (`live_node_manager`).
+- B5's escalation pointer is therefore delivered from the production `/seat` entry point.
+
+Step 3 has two gaps against the baseline and §4.12:
+- Manager duty. The human request includes "managers are tasked with listening, detecting, unblocking", and §4.12 requires a `reports` list in the reply with a skill step that tells a session with reports that it is their manager. At head the reply has no `reports` field (seat_reply builds only `manager` and `node_manager`) and the skill has no such step. A session that manages other seats is never told so, so the listening half of the hierarchy has no producer. Open bead hg-k4l.19 owns it, but no human scope change row covers it.
+- Node manager self-escalation. For the node manager seat, `manager_chain` is empty, so `manager` is null and `node_manager` names the session's own seat. Step 3 then tells the node manager to escalate lifecycle issues to itself, not to the user. This contradicts B8 ("node managers dont have a parent") and §4.12 ("when the session's own seat is the node manager, the reply and skill say so and carry the node-manager duties"). hg-k4l.19 also owns the reply and skill half of this; the shared duty text depends on hg-k4l.14 (templates/node-manager/AGENTS.md), which is also open.
+
+## Requirement baseline trace for this cluster
+
+- B2 and B3: delivered. The exit-5 line from cli::daemon_error plus the skill's exit-5 branch tell the session to retry later and carry on.
+- B4 (integrity distinct from transient): the skill side is delivered by the exit-6 branch. Producing the integrity error is the bootstrap/daemon clusters' path.
+- B5: delivered for "each session knows its manager". The listening/unblocking duty stated in the same human request is not delivered (see the first item under Must fix).
+- B8: the skill text breaks it for the node manager session, which is told to escalate to itself (second item under Must fix).
+- B10: the shipped node-manager/office templates are not in the range at all (hg-k4l.14 open). No cluster contains them, so the seam reviewer has to trace this; it is listed here for visibility, not judged as this cluster's file.
+- B11: documented by the CURRENT-DESIGN line, which matches classify/reconcile at head. Behaviour delivery belongs to the observe/reconcile cluster.
+- B1, B6, B7, B9, B12, B13, B14: no artifact in this cluster carries them. Other clusters own them.
+
+## Verdict
+not ready (seat skill and reply give managers no reports/duty step and send the node manager to escalate to itself; hg-k4l.19 open)
+
+## Must fix before landing
+- Human request "managers are tasked with listening, detecting, unblocking" (spec §4.12, B5 discussion) is not delivered at head: seat_reply in src/bootstrap/mod.rs emits no `reports` field and skills/seat/SKILL.md has no step telling a session with reports that it must listen for, detect and unblock their lifecycle issues, so no production path informs a manager seat of its duty (open bead hg-k4l.19; no human scope change row covers it).
+- skills/seat/SKILL.md step 3 sends the node manager to escalate to itself: for the node manager seat `manager` is null (empty manager_chain) and `node_manager` names its own seat, so "when it is null, go to the `node_manager`" points it at itself instead of the user, contrary to B8 and spec §4.12 ("when the session's own seat is the node manager, the reply and skill say so and carry the node-manager duties"); the duty text shared with templates/node-manager/AGENTS.md also does not exist (hg-k4l.19, hg-k4l.14 open).
+
+## Untested scope
+- No test pins the new skills/seat/SKILL.md failure branch (exit 5 / exit 6 / other) or the step 3 escalation text; seat_skill_has_instruction_steps in src/bootstrap/tests.rs checks only the Codex fallback, `instructions.text` and `data` lines, so an edit that drops the failure step would pass (HOOK_PROMPT's clause is pinned in src/cli/seat.rs:240, the skill's target of that clause is not).
+- No test ties the skill's exit-6 wording ("the node manager seat the line names, or the user when the line says so") to the three node_manager_suffix forms; wording drift between src/bootstrap/mod.rs and the skill is not caught.
+
+## Deferred OK
+- CURRENT-DESIGN.md has only the §4.9 dated closure-exemption line; the fuller dated section (manager precedence, first seat, reparent and its undo, exit codes 2/5/6, fallback removal) and README exit-code docs are tracked by open bead hg-k4l.20 and are a documentation criterion beyond the spec's §4.9 requirement.
+- The exit-5 line's "ask your manager or coordinator" is shown to a seat whose /seat failed and so has no loaded manager reference; spec §4.4 prescribes this exact text and the skill's "carry on" instruction keeps the session safe.
+- .gitignore `.superpowers/` entry is workflow housekeeping with no tracked paths affected.
